BCC_Q({"y": 2021, "n": 12, "part": "C", "topic": "graph", "title": "Unlock the Crown", "answer": 2, "story": "<p>A crown <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:3cm\"/> is locked in one of\n15 drawers as shown.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p><img alt=\"Drawers arranged into 3  rows and 5 columns. A description of the drawers can found at the end of the Story.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:80.0%\"/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>There is a keyhole at the top of each drawer. To open the drawer, you\nmust insert an object with the same shape as the keyhole. For example,\nfor the keyhole <img alt=\"shaped like a diamond\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:1cm\"/> on the top left drawer, you must insert an object shaped like a\ndiamond.<\/p>\n<p>Each drawer contains one object as indicated on the front of the\ndrawer below the keyhole. For example, the top left drawer contains an\nobject shaped like a heart <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:1cm\"/>.<\/p>\n<button onclick=\"hideSeek('longdesc3')\" style=\"box-shadow:none\">Hide/Reveal Description of Drawers<\/button>\n<div id=\"longdesc3\" style=\"display:none\">\n<p>For each drawer, the object in the drawer and the keyhole shape on the drawer are given in the following table. The drawers are presented in the order in which they appear in the three by five grid, going from left to right along each row.\n<table>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Drawer<\/th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Object<br/>(in drawer)<\/th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Keyhole shape<br/>(on drawer)<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">heart<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">diamond<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">tree<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">star<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">cross<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">heart<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">4<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">moon<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">star<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">5<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">heart<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">circle<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">6<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">cross<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">pentagon<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">7<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">pentagon<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">circle<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">8<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">crown<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">moon<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">9<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">tree<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">diamond<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">10<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">star<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">triangle<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">11<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">tree<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">cross<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">12<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">diamond<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">heart<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">13<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">star<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">square<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">14<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">heart<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">triangle<\/td>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">15<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">triangle<\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">pentagon<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/tr><\/table>\n<hr class=\"longdesc\"/>\n<\/p><\/div>", "question": "<p>Bella has an object shaped like a circle. What is the minimum number\nof drawers that Bella needs to open in order to retrieve the crown?<\/p>\n<ol class=\"mc\">\n<li>3<\/li>\n<li>4<\/li>\n<li>5<\/li>\n<li>6<\/li>\n<\/ol>", "answerHtml": "<p>(C) 5<\/p>", "explanation": "<p>Working backwards from the drawer with the crown, we can determine\nwhich drawers Bella must open to retrieve the crown.<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>To retrieve the crown, Bella must open the middle drawer. This\nmeans she needs to retrieve a moon.\n<div class=\"center\">\n<img alt=\"A crown locked behind a moon-shaped keyhole. \" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:10.0%\"/>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<li>From #1, we know Bella must open the drawer containing a moon.\nThis means she needs to retrieve a star.\n<div class=\"center\">\n<img alt=\"A moon locked behind a star-shaped keyhole. \" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:10.0%\"/>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<li>From #2, we know Bella must open one of the two drawers\ncontaining a star. This means she needs to retrieve either a square or a\ntriangle. Since there are no drawers containing a square, she needs to\nretrieve a triangle.\n<div class=\"center\">\n<img alt=\"A star locked behind a square-shaped keyhole. \" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:10.0%\"/>\n<img alt=\"A star locked behind a triangle-shaped keyhole. \" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:10.0%\"/>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<li>From #3, we know Bella must open the drawer containing a\ntriangle. This means she needs to retrieve a pentagon.\n<div class=\"center\">\n<img alt=\"A triangle locked behind a pentagon-shaped keyhole. \" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:10.0%\"/>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<li>From #4, we know Bella must open the drawer containing a\npentagon. She can do this using the circle she began with.\n<div class=\"center\">\n<img alt=\"A pentagon locked behind a circle-shaped keyhole. \" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:10.0%\"/>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>This work tells us that Bella must open at least 5 drawers in order\nto retrieve the crown. It also tells us that the 5 drawers highlighted\nin the following diagram can be used to retrieve the crown in the order\nindicated. Therefore, 5 is the minimum number of drawers that Bella\nneeds to open.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p><img alt=\"The five drawers in order: pentagon behind circle-shaped keyhole, triangle behind pentagon-shaped keyhole, star behind triangle-shaped keyhole, moon behind star-shaped keyhole, and crown behind moon-shaped keyhole.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:50.0%\"/><\/p>\n<\/div>", "connections": "<p>The ways in which each drawer can be opened can be modelled by a\n<em>directed graph<\/em>. We can represent each drawer as a\n<em>vertex<\/em> of the directed graph. Each <em>(directed) edge<\/em>\nwill go from a drawer with a certain symbol to a drawer with the keyhole\nmatching that symbol. In the diagram, the edges are\n<span><em>implicit<\/em><\/span>, since they are not actually part of the\npicture, but are rather inferred from the information available on each\ndrawer.<\/p>\n<p>The reason we say the graph is “directed\" is because the opening of a\ndrawer is only valid in one direction. For example, if drawer A contains\na symbol that opens the keyhole of drawer B, we would have a directed\nedge from drawer A to drawer B, and it is not necessarily the case that\nthe symbol in drawer B opens the keyhole for drawer A. In this case, we\ncall B a <span><em>neighbour<\/em><\/span> of A.<\/p>\n<p>In this problem, we want to find a <span><em>directed\npath<\/em><\/span> to the crown. One way to solve this is to perform a\n<span><em>breadth-first search<\/em><\/span>, where all of the neighbours\nof the crown are determined, and then repeatedly determine the\nneighbours of each of those neighbours, and so on.<\/p>\n<p>The idea of searching for a path in a directed graph has many\napplications, such as mapping out a driving route, determining how to\nsend information through the internet, and determining recommendations\nfor who you may want to connect with on social media platforms.<\/p>", "mc": 1});